# Example ReRDMFT input file: stretched LiH (5 Angstrom), 6-31G, GNOF (two coupling subspaces),
# FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE with X2C and C4_SPINOR in one run -- the 4-component counterpart of
# lih_X2C_gnof_full_optimization_dissociated.inp. C4_SPINOR's orbital rotations are restricted to
# the positive-energy spinors only (see README.md, "FULL_OPTIMIZATION for C4_SPINOR"), so the
# X2C and 4-component energies can be compared directly on this near-degenerate case.
# Stretched LiH has near-degenerate SCF solutions: DIIS (the default) converges to a higher one than
# the damped linear density mixing, so use the mixing (DIIS FALSE), as in the X2C example.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
X2C TRUE
C4_SPINOR TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
MACRO_ENERGY_TOLERANCE 1e-10
DIIS FALSE

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   5.000000
END
